From 8fca9c4b2640ad1f4dcb5b2ea5d12ad51c146fda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: energie-teilen <noreply@energie-teilen.de>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:38:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: audit findings across security, legal surface,
 accessibility and delivery
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A full audit of the product with real tooling, and every defect it found.

SECURITY
- No browser-hardening headers were sent at all. Adds a CSP written for this
  application's actual dependencies (no unsafe-inline for script, no eval),
  plus nosniff, frame-ancestors none, referrer policy, permissions policy,
  COOP/CORP and HSTS in production.
- The Stripe webhook answered 200 "ok" to a forged signature whenever Stripe
  was unconfigured — a fake success that also caused genuine deliveries to be
  discarded instead of retried. It now answers 503.
- Missing assets fell through to the SPA shell, so a missing font returned
  index.html with status 200 and the browser reported a decode error rather
  than a missing file. Asset paths now 404.

HEALTH
- /api/health reported ok:true on a deployment that could not take a payment
  or send an email. The verdict is now derived from the capabilities the
  funnel needs, and a degraded response names each missing one and what it
  costs.

LEGAL SURFACE
- The imprint, privacy notice and terms shipped with thirteen bracketed
  placeholders and with notes addressed to the operator ("Strukturentwurf.
  Vor Veröffentlichung anwaltlich prüfen lassen") rendered to visitors.
  All three now read from shared/legal-entity.ts, state honestly that the
  details are being added while the record is incomplete, and a release gate
  blocks a production deploy until it is filled.
- The three pages rendered with no header and no footer, outside the site's
  information architecture. They now use a shared layout with breadcrumbs.
- The 404 page was untouched scaffolding: English copy on a German product,
  a foreign colour palette, and a button where a link belongs.

PRIVACY
- Web fonts were loaded from a third-party CDN, transmitting every visitor's
  IP address before any consent and putting a cross-origin request on the
  critical path. Fonts are now declared locally, with scripts/fetch-fonts.mjs
  to populate them and a guard that fails the build if an external font host
  returns.

ACCESSIBILITY
- A range input reached assistive technology unnamed.
- Offer cards nested a button inside an ARIA radio; they now use a real,
  visually hidden radio input, so group semantics and arrow-key navigation
  come from the platform.
- Five scrollable regions could not be reached or scrolled by keyboard.
- Muted text on the legal pages failed the contrast threshold.
- No skip link existed.
- Entrance animations ignored prefers-reduced-motion; only CSS transitions
  honoured it.

DELIVERY
- /rechner and /pilot dropped their hash, so a shared deep link landed at the
  top of the page instead of at the section it named.
- recharts was named as a manual chunk, which put the largest bundle in the
  build into the first paint. Charts are now split AND deferred until they
  approach the viewport, because splitting alone does not help on a page
  where everything renders at once.

SUPPLY CHAIN
- Removed 30 production dependencies and 48 unreachable UI components: six
  packages were never referenced at all, and 24 Radix packages existed only
  for components nothing rendered. 58 production dependencies down to 28.
- Removed leftover storage-proxy scaffolding referencing an unrelated service.

VERIFICATION
- Playwright suite over Chromium desktop, mobile and tablet: route
  reachability, the navigation graph, browser history, calculator controls
  and persistence, every engine panel, lead capture including API failure,
  axe accessibility on every route, security headers, secret exposure,
  injection, rate limiting, and performance budgets. 270 checks.
- Build guards for each defect above, so none can return quietly.
- CI split into verify / e2e / release, with traces and reports uploaded on
  failure, a dependency audit, and an SPDX-evaluating licence check.
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/RUNBOOK.md.

507 unit tests and 270 browser checks pass. Typecheck and build clean.
